.SH CONFIGURATION
dm reads $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/dm/config.kdl, or $HOME/.config/dm/config.kdl when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset. A missing file means the built-in values; dm writes a default file on first run. The file is a patch over the built-in values: a node the file leaves out keeps its built-in value. The nodes are:
.TP
\fBprefix\fP
Value: \fIa quoted key name, one sequence\fP. Default: \fI"ctrl+b"\fP.
Set the prefix key that opens the main keymap.
.TP
\fBdefault-fold\fP
Value: \fI"fold" or "unfold"\fP. Default: \fI"unfold"\fP.
Set whether a new window's rail starts folded or unfolded. A reload applies it to windows created after it.
.TP
\fBtab-min-width\fP
Value: \fIan integer of at least 3 cells\fP. Default: \fI8\fP.
Set the smallest tab width in the window tab bar.
.TP
\fBtab-max-width\fP
Value: \fIan integer of at least 3 cells, not below tab-min-width\fP. Default: \fI20\fP.
Set the largest tab width before the label is cut.
.TP
\fBpadding\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 0 to 4 cells\fP. Default: \fI0\fP.
Set the blank cells between a pane's border and its content. A reload resizes every pane.
.TP
\fBhistory-lines\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 100 to 32768 lines\fP. Default: \fI10000\fP.
Set the scrollback window and the pane ring budget: about 256 bytes per line, capped at 8 MiB.
.TP
\fBglyphs\fP
Value: \fI"auto", "ascii", "unicode" or "nerd"\fP. Default: \fI"auto"\fP.
Choose the glyph vocabulary the chrome draws with.
.TP
\fBwindow-label\fP
Value: \fIa quoted Go template\fP. Default: \fI"{{if .Named}}{{.Name}}{{else}}{{.ID}}{{with base .Root}} {{.}}{{end}}{{end}}"\fP.
Set the template that renders a window label.
.TP
\fBdashboard-preview\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 0 to 100\fP. Default: \fI40\fP.
Set the share of the dashboard body the preview band opens at. Zero opens on the table alone; the peek key still shows the band.
.TP
\fBpalette-rows\fP
Value: \fIan integer of at least 1\fP. Default: \fI10\fP.
Set how many entries the command palette shows before it scrolls. A screen too small for the cap holds fewer.
.TP
\fBask-rows\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 8 to 64\fP. Default: \fI30\fP.
Set the fewest interior rows the ask float reserves. The detail pane fills the rows the floor leaves, so a taller box reads more of a long description or preview before it elides.
.TP
\fBask-cols\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 40 to 240\fP. Default: \fI96\fP.
Set the widest the ask float may stand, in columns. The float still keeps six columns clear of the screen edge, so a value wider than the terminal only uses what is there.
.TP
\fBask-split\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 20 to 80\fP. Default: \fI60\fP.
Set the share of the ask box's width the detail column takes, in percent. The options are labels on one row each, so the detail column, which carries the description and the preview, takes the larger half.
.TP
\fBdiff-command\fP
Value: \fIa quoted shell command\fP. Default: \fI"hunk diff"\fP.
Set the command the dashboard diff key runs in a floating pane, or in a split pane with the dashboard's diff-split key. It runs through sh -c in the selected pane folder.
.TP
\fBweb-addr\fP
Value: \fIa quoted host:port, as in "100.71.227.52:8099"\fP. Default: \fI"127.0.0.1:8099"\fP.
Set the host:port dm web listens on. It applies only when --addr is not passed, so an explicit flag always wins. An absent or empty node keeps the loopback default; a value that is not host:port is refused when the config loads.
.TP
\fBdashboard-layout\fP
Value: \fI"full" or "float"\fP. Default: \fI"float"\fP.
Draw the dashboard over the whole screen, or as a palette centred over the panes.
.TP
\fBdashboard-peek\fP
Value: \fI"right" or "down"\fP. Default: \fI"down"\fP.
Set where the dashboard preview band sits: under the table, or beside it on the right. The peek key still shows and hides the band.
.TP
\fBshelf-layout\fP
Value: \fI"centered" or "pane"\fP. Default: \fI"centered"\fP.
Place the summoned shelf as a centred tray over the pane area, or over the focused pane. The rail, the tab bar and the status bar stay visible in both.
.TP
\fBshelf-size\fP
Value: \fIan integer from 20 to 100\fP. Default: \fI80\fP.
Set the share of the pane area a centred shelf takes, in percent. The strip and at least three rows of screen are always kept.
.TP
\fBfloat-shadow\fP
Value: \fI"off" or "on"\fP. Default: \fI"off"\fP.
Set the drop shadow the floats paint beside and under their box: the prefix help box, the rename prompt and every floating pane.
.TP
\fBtheme\fP
Value: \fIa quoted theme name matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]+\fP. Default: none.
Select a theme from the themes directory beside config.kdl; no node keeps the built-in theme.
.TP
\fBkeymap\fP
Value: \fIa quoted mode name and a { "action" "key" } block\fP. Default: \fIthe built-in table\fP.
Patch one keymap mode; an action the file leaves out keeps its built-in key.
.TP
\fBcommand\fP
Value: \fIa quoted name matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ and a { run "..." } block\fP. Default: \fInone\fP.
Define a command a keymap can run: bind "command:<name>" to a key and it runs the run text through sh -c in the window's folder.
.TP
\fBplugin\fP
Value: \fIa quoted name matching [A-Za-z0-9_-]+ and a { exec ... where ... } block\fP. Default: \fInone\fP.
Declare a plugin: bind "plugin:<name>" to a key and it opens the exec argv in a split or window pane, in its folder, with its env.
